 {"id":"fabro-696c","title":"Fix PR publishing: provision a PR-capable credential or disable PRs","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T19:13:30.865Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-02T19:13:30.865Z","description":"Two git.push events succeeded with token_provenance: static, then PR creation returned 403 (deterministic, retry-proof), while .fabro/project.toml line 59 states PR creation requires the GitHub App integration the static token lacks (run 01M0SFEYVC9TD6MP816RHEBFQY). Provision that credential or set enabled = false under [run.pull_request] until it exists. Effect: publish stops being the sole cause of failed runs; with a preflight the failure would surface in seconds instead of after the full 2m41s workflow."}
 {"id":"fabro-a54d","title":"Make the baked mise toolchain a no-op in run containers","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T19:13:36.182Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-02T19:13:36.182Z","description":"Run 01M0SFEYVC9TD6MP816RHEBFQY: mise install took 95.5s (61% of end-to-end) re-installing tool versions Dockerfile.mise already bakes, likely because MISE_DATA_DIR=/mise is not honored in the run container; .mise.toml's header also still claims 'no baked-in tools', contradicting project.toml. Fix env propagation in .fabro/Dockerfile.mise and [run.prepare] in .fabro/project.toml, add mise ls output to the prepare log when install exceeds a few seconds, and update the stale .mise.toml header. Related to fabro-80ec (pre-install toolset in runner image) but targets env propagation and stale docs. Effect: ~95s saved on every run; setup stops dominating run time."}
